1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
So AI, LLM AI,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,210
is a mode-seeking device.

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:09,900
The tricky thing is this:

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:14,900
if you want the tail of the distribution,

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:19,450
something way out on the right tail,

6
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:22,180
and you ask AI for that...

7
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,420
you get a modal answer, regardless.

8
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:29,120
If you want to find the mode

9
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:33,900
faster, cheaper and more accurately,

10
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,000
use AI.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,350
If you want something on the tail, don't.

12
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:40,870
It's not set up to do that.

13
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,460
I don't like the idea

14
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:47,960
of giving your problem set to AI and asking:

15
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:50,780
“What should my strategy be?”

16
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:52,540
You'll get a modal strategy.

17
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,860
If you're doing what everybody else is doing,

18
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:58,300
it's not distinctive. It's not worth having.
